			],
			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Remove Effect-TS Ref/PubSub overhead in ExtensionService, WindowService, and Event Stream\n\nReplace Effect.Ref and Effect.PubSub with plain JavaScript Maps and variables where reactive semantics are not required. This eliminates unnecessary Effect runtime overhead on hot paths like extension lookup, window state access, and event firing.\n\nKey modifications:\n- ExtensionService: Three Ref<Map> instances replaced with plain Maps (_registry, _activation, _exports). MarkActivated/MarkDeactivated now use Effect.sync with direct Map mutations instead of Ref.update + Effect.gen.\n- WindowService: Ref<WindowState> replaced with a plain let variable. State getter and AcceptWindowStateChange now access _windowState directly.\n- CreateEventStream: Removed PubSub entirely; Fire now directly calls VSCodeEmitter.fire via Effect.sync. Shutdown only disposes the emitter.\n- ESBuild and Mountain configurations: Expanded with descriptive names, validation functions, and JSDoc-style comments (continuing from ede8662).\n- Source/Generated/RouteManifest.ts: Timestamp regenerated to 2026-06-11T02:01:37Z.\n- Source/Codegen/Emit/Emit/Ext/Host/Schema.ts: Minor @ts-ignore comment formatting.\n- Source/ESBuild.js: Inline config aligned with expanded Configuration/ESBuild structure.\n\nImpact: Reduced Effect-TS allocation overhead on extension lifecycle, window state tracking, and event emission paths. Configuration files are now self-documenting.",
			"SHA": "72d3ebd674788432d548c4fd270c78aab7ea53d1"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-11T02:22:55Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1198,
				36
			],
			"Message": "fix(Cocoon): Guard window.didChangeActiveTextEditor emission against undefined editor\n\nThe notification handler for `onDidChangeActiveTextEditor` was unconditionally emitting the `window.didChangeActiveTextEditor` event with an undefined editor stub when no editor was active. Many VS Code extensions contain buggy optional chaining like `n?.document.languageId` (missing the second `?.`) which throws \"Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'languageId')\" when the editor is undefined.\n\nAdd a conditional check to only emit the event when a valid TextEditorStub exists, matching VS Code's behavior of firing with undefined to signal \"no active editor\" while protecting incompatible extensions from crashing.\n\nRouteManifest timestamp regenerated as part of the build cycle.",
			"SHA": "e7da10863358cde9b1b2247ce0f3e6569e7f8437"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-10T20:23:34Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠃⠀⠀⠀",
				1198,
				300
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Cocoon): Expand ESBuild and Mountain configurations for readability\n\nThe ESBuild configuration files in Configuration/ESBuild/ and the Mountain gRPC configuration in Configuration/Mountain/Config.js were previously minified with single-letter variables and compressed formatting. This change expands all configuration files to use descriptive variable names, proper formatting, meaningful comments, and structured exports.\n\nKey modifications:\n- Configuration/ESBuild/: All config files (Bootstrap.js, Cocoon.js, Base/Config.js, Bootstrap/Config.js, Compile/Config.js, Target/Config.js, Constant/Environment/Constant.js, Target.js, index.js) rewritten with clear naming (Environment, BootstrapConfig, CocoonESBuildConfig, TargetConfig, Merge, TierDefines) and explanatory comments for complex logic like the banner injection for CJS require shim and outdir/outbase conflict avoidance.\n- Configuration/Mountain/Config.js: Complete rewrite adding named functions (loadMountainConfigFromEnv, validateMountainConfig, createMountainConfig, getMountainConfigSummary) with JSDoc-style structure, proper validation logic, and configuration summary output.\n- Source/Generated/RouteManifest.ts: Routine timestamp regeneration (2026-06-10T20:14:00Z).\n- Target/: Compiled artifacts regenerated as expected from the configuration changes.\n\nImpact: Build configuration is now self-documenting and maintainable, eliminating the need for external documentation to understand ESBuild options and Mountain gRPC client settings.",
			"SHA": "ede8662feae3a7be7dd4001592c7001fcbf1ed53"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-10T20:22:25Z",
